===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|smokyng}}, {{m|enm|smokynge}}, equivalent to {{af|en|smoke|-ing}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act or process of [[emit]]ting smoke.
# The burning and [[inhalation]] of [[tobacco]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Smoking''' can lead to lung cancer.}}
#* '''2012''', Montgomery J. Granger, ''Saving Grace at Guantanamo Bay: A Memoir of a Citizen Warrior''
#*: He had the loudest voice of any drill sergeant, and seemed to enjoy the group '''smokings''' as well as the individual smokings.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The burning and inhalation of other substances, e.g. marijuana.
# The act of exposing (something) to smoke; {{lb|en|by extension}} the process by which foods are cured or flavoured by smoke
# {{lb|en|slang|obsolete}} A [[banter]]ing; [[teasing]]; [[mockery]].

